<div class="ind-flow ind-section ind-section--inset:start-collapse" data-component-id="ind2:section">
      
                                                      
      


  <p class="ind-paragraph--lead">On this page you will find the required amounts per residence permit. Your income should at least be equal to the required amount for the residence permit you are applying for.</p>


      
      
          
      </div>

  

                        
  






<section class="ind-flow ind-section ind-section--inset:start-collapse" data-component-id="ind2:section">
      
                              




<h2 id="you-are-the-sponsor-for-a-short-stay-schengen-visa-or-visa-exempt-period" data-component-id="ind2:heading" class="ind-heading ind-heading--h2">
      You are the sponsor for a short stay (Schengen visa or visa-exempt period)
  </h2>

  
  

  
  

  <p>These required amounts are valid from 1 July 2026 up to and including 31 December 2026.</p><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 2,337.00</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month with&nbsp;holiday allowance</td><td>€ 2,523.96</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits) are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p>

<div class="ind:clear-both"></div>




          
      </section>


  






<section class="ind-flow ind-section" data-component-id="ind2:section">
      
                              




<h2 id="application-for-a-residence-permit-to-stay-with-family-member" data-component-id="ind2:heading" class="ind-heading ind-heading--h2">
      Application for a residence permit to stay with family member
  </h2>

  
  

  
  

  <p>These required amounts are valid from 1 July 2026 up to and including 31 December 2026.</p><h3>Residence permit to stay with a partner​</h3><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 2,337.00</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 2,523.96</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p><h3>Residence permit to stay with another family member​</h3><h4>The sponsor is married/registered partner or an unmarried couple living together​</h4><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 2,337.00</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 2,523.96</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p><h4>The sponsor is a single parent</h4><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 1,635.90</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 1,766.77</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p><p>Are you currently a single parent and also applying for a residence permit for your partner? Then the higher required amount applies. So, the required amount for a sponsor who is married, a registered partner, or living together unmarried.</p>

<div class="ind:clear-both"></div>




          
      </section>


  






<section class="ind-flow ind-section" data-component-id="ind2:section">
      
                              




<h2 id="application-for-a-residence-permit-for-study" data-component-id="ind2:heading" class="ind-heading ind-heading--h2">
      Application for a residence permit for study
  </h2>

  
  

  
  

  <h3>Study amounts 2026</h3><p>These amounts are valid from 1 January 2026 up to and including 31 December 2026.</p><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Study type</th><th scope="col">Monthly amount</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Higher professional education (hbo) or university</td><td>€ 1,130.77</td></tr><tr><td>Secondary education or senior secondary vocational education (mbo)</td><td>€ 928.58</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>A person in the Netherlands finances the study and stay of the student</h3><p>These required amounts are valid from 1 July 2026 up to and including 31 December 2026.</p><h4>Higher professional education (hbo) or university students</h4><h5>​​The financier is married/registered partner or an unmarried couple living together&nbsp;​ ​</h5><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 3,467.77</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV&nbsp;salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 3,654.73</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p><h5>The financier is single or a single parent</h5><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 2,766.67</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV&nbsp;salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 2,897.54</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p><h4>​​Secondary education or senior secondary vocational education (mbo)​ students</h4><h5>The financier is married/registered partner or an unmarried couple living together &nbsp;​ ​</h5><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 3,265.58</td></tr><tr><td>​​​Gross SV&nbsp;salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 3,452.54</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p><h5>The financier is single or a single parent</h5><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 2,564.48</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV&nbsp;salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 2,695.35</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p>

<div class="ind:clear-both"></div>




          
      </section>


  






<section class="ind-flow ind-section" data-component-id="ind2:section">
      
                              




<h2 id="application-for-a-residence-permit-to-work-in-paid-employment-or-for-seasonal-work" data-component-id="ind2:heading" class="ind-heading ind-heading--h2">
      Application for a residence permit to work in paid employment or for seasonal work
  </h2>

  
  

  
  

  <p>These required amounts are valid from 1 July 2026 up to and including 31 December 2026.</p><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 2,337.00</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 2,523.96</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p>

<div class="ind:clear-both"></div>


  

  <h3><a class="ck-anchor" id="income-amounts-arts-culture"></a>Application for a residence permit to work in paid employment in specific occupations in arts and culture</h3><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Occupation</th><th scope="col">Gross SV salary per month</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Leader 2nd violins, violas and double basses</td><td>€ 2,383</td></tr><tr><td>Actor</td><td>€ 4,233</td></tr><tr><td>​Artistic (deputy) director dance/musical/cultural workshop</td><td>€ 2,987</td></tr><tr><td>Artistic leader or artistic advisor music/opera</td><td>€ 4,020</td></tr><tr><td>​Artistic project coordinator cultural workshop</td><td>€ 2,118</td></tr><tr><td>Choreographer</td><td>€ 3,200</td></tr><tr><td>Dancer/musical artist</td><td>€ 2,039</td></tr><tr><td>Conductor</td><td>€ 4,000</td></tr><tr><td>​First orchestra leader</td><td>€ 4,077</td></tr><tr><td>First player or soloist wind section, first harpist and first timpanist</td><td>€ 2,383</td></tr><tr><td>Core guidance cultural workshop departments</td><td>€ 2,536</td></tr><tr><td>Designer (including scenic design, costumes, light, sound, video)</td><td>€ 1,921</td></tr><tr><td>Deputy first orchestra leader</td><td>€ 2,683</td></tr><tr><td>Director</td><td>€ 4,233</td></tr><tr><td>Soloist music/opera</td><td>€ 4,000</td></tr><tr><td>Soloist cellist</td><td>€ 3,017</td></tr><tr><td>Technical (project) specialist cultural workshop</td><td>€ 2,118</td></tr><tr><td>Singer/musical artist</td><td>€ 2,971</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p>

<div class="ind:clear-both"></div>




          
      </section>


  






<section class="ind-flow ind-section" data-component-id="ind2:section">
      
                              




<h2 id="application-for-a-residence-permit-for-an-internship-or-as-a-trainee" data-component-id="ind2:heading" class="ind-heading ind-heading--h2">
      Application for a residence permit for an internship or as a trainee
  </h2>

  
  

  
  

  <p>These required amounts are valid from 1 July 2026 up to and including 31 December 2026.</p><h3>Trainee</h3><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 2,337.00</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 2,523.96</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p><h3>Internship</h3><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 1,168.50</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV&nbsp;salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 1,261.98</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>Is an internship allowance mentioned in the internship agreement? Then this internship allowance may be included.<br><br>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p><h3>Application for a residence permit action programme of the European Union</h3><p>These required amounts are valid from 1 July 2026 up to and including 31 December 2026.</p><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 1,168.50</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV&nbsp;salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 1,261.98</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p>

<div class="ind:clear-both"></div>




          
      </section>


  






<section class="ind-flow ind-section" data-component-id="ind2:section">
      
                              




<h2 id="application-to-work-as-a-highly-skilled-migrant-and-for-the-european-blue-card" data-component-id="ind2:heading" class="ind-heading ind-heading--h2">
      Application to work as a highly skilled migrant and for the European Blue Card
  </h2>

  
  

  
  

  <h3>Required amount for a highly skilled migrant/European Blue Card for first application, extension or change of employer (sponsor)</h3><p>The required amounts change every year on January 1. The highly skilled migrant must meet the required amount that applies on the date of the application. Does the highly skilled migrant change employers? The highly skilled migrant must then meet the required amount applicable on the date on which the employment contract with the new employer commences. More information can be found in the brochure&nbsp;</p>  



      <figure>
  
  
  
  


<a rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" data-component-id="ind2:link" class="ind-link" href="/en/forms/3072.pdf">
        



<span data-component-id="ind2:icon" class="ind-icon" aria-hidden="true">
  <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="icon icon-tabler icons-tabler-outline icon-tabler-file-description ind-icon__svg" aria-hidden="true">
  <path stroke="none" d="M0 0h24v24H0z" fill="none" /><path d="M14 3v4a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h4" /><path d="M17 21h-10a2 2 0 0 1 -2 -2v-14a2 2 0 0 1 2 -2h7l5 5v11a2 2 0 0 1 -2 2z" /><path d="M9 17h6" /><path d="M9 13h6" />
</svg>
</span>

      Residence permit for work as a highly skilled migrant (PDF, 639.86 KB)
    </a>

      </figure>
  

<h3>Type of highly skilled migrant/European Blue Card with the right required amount (gross per month) for 2026</h3><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Type highly skilled migrant/European Blue Card</th><th scope="col">First residence permit highly skilled migrant/European Blue Card</th><th scope="col">Application extension residence permit highly skilled migrant/European Blue Card for the same employer</th><th scope="col">When changing employer (sponsor);</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Highly skilled migrants <a href="#reduced-salary-criterion">reduced salary criterion</a></th><td>€ 3,122.00</td><td>€ 3,122.00</td><td>€ 3,122.00</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Highly skilled migrants younger than 30 years</th><td>€ 4,357.00</td><td><p>€ 4,357.00</p><p><br>This amount also applies when the highly skilled migrant has turned 30 years or older.</p><p>Has the highly skilled migrant changed employers since the first permit was issued? Then this must have happened when the highly skilled migrant was still under the age of 30.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><ul><li>Highly skilled migrant is still younger than 30:<br>€ 4,357.00<br>&nbsp;</li><li>Highly skilled migrant is now 30 years or older:<br>€ 5,942.00</li></ul></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Highly skilled migrants 30 years or older</th><td>€ 5,942.00</td><td>€ 5,942.00</td><td>€ 5,942.00</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">​European Blue Card</th><td>€ 5,942.00</td><td>€ 5,942.00</td><td>€ 5,942.00</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Reduced salary criterion European Blue Card</th><td>€ 4,754.00</td><td>€ 4,754.00</td><td>€ 4,754.00</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3><a class="ck-anchor" id="reduced-salary-criterion"></a>Reduced salary criterion</h3><p>The reduced salary criterion applies in these 3 cases:</p><ol><li>The residence permit for a highly skilled migrant is applied for during the residence permit for an orientation year for highly educated persons.</li><li>The highly skilled migrant no longer has a residence permit for an orientation year for highly educated persons, but did have this permit. The residence permit for a highly skilled migrant is applied for within 3 years of the graduation date or date of the doctoral defence ceremony. Or it is applied for within 3 years of the date on which the residence permit for research expired.</li><li>The highly skilled migrant has never had a residence permit for an orientation year for highly educated persons, but does meet the requirements for that residence purpose. For example because the highly skilled migrant has graduated, obtained a doctoral degree or has done research. The application for the residence permit for a highly skilled migrant must be submitted within 3 years of the graduation date or date of the doctoral defence ceremony. Or it must be submitted within 3 years of the date on which the residence permit for research expired.</li></ol><p>Read more about the <a href="/en/residence-permits/work/residence-permit-for-orientation-year" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="0718cad0-5109-4b21-8b1b-2e4a43005597" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="Residence permit for orientation year">residence permit for an orientation year for highly educated persons</a>.</p><h3>Reduced salary criterion European Blue Card</h3><p>The reduced EU Blue Card salary criterion applies to graduates who have completed a higher education programme. The (recognised) sponsor should apply for the European Blue Card residence permit within 3 years after the graduation or promotion date.&nbsp;<br>The lower salary criterion may also apply if you extend the residence permit or change your employer within 3 years after graduation or promotion. Or if you apply for an extension within 24 months after obtaining the first residence permit European Blue Card.</p><h3>What may be included in the salary criterion?</h3><p>The IND counts the reimbursements of expenses and fixed allowances (such as a thirteenth month) in the salary criterion. For this the following conditions apply:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>The reimbursements and allowances are in the contract.</li><li>The employer transfers the reimbursements and allowances to a bank account in name of the highly skilled migrant or holder of the European blue card.</li><li>The employer transfers the reimbursement and allowances each month. This means that the employer pays the thirteenth month monthly in 12 equal amounts.</li></ul><p>The following pay elements are not included in the salary criterion:</p><ul><li>Vacation allowance.</li><li>The value of payment made in kind.</li><li>Uncertain, non-regular pay elements (for example overtime allowances, tips and payments from funds).</li></ul>

<div class="ind:clear-both"></div>




          
      </section>


  






<section class="ind-flow ind-section" data-component-id="ind2:section">
      
                              




<h2 id="application-for-a-residence-permit-as-a-researcher-guest-lecturer-or-physician-in-training-to-be-a-specialist" data-component-id="ind2:heading" class="ind-heading ind-heading--h2">
      Application for a residence permit as a researcher, guest lecturer or physician in training to be a specialist
  </h2>

  
  

  
  

  <p>This required amounts also apply for a residence permit highly skilled migrant. These amounts are valid from 1 July 2026 up to and including 31 December 2026.</p><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 1,635.90</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 1,766.77</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p>

<div class="ind:clear-both"></div>




          
      </section>


  






<section class="ind-flow ind-section" data-component-id="ind2:section">
      
                              




<h2 id="application-for-a-residence-permit-as-essential-start-up-personnel" data-component-id="ind2:heading" class="ind-heading ind-heading--h2">
      Application for a residence permit as essential start-up personnel
  </h2>

  
  

  
  

  <h3>Required amount 2026</h3><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross income per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 3,122.00</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<div class="ind:clear-both"></div>




          
      </section>


  






<section class="ind-flow ind-section" data-component-id="ind2:section">
      
                              




<h2 id="application-for-a-residence-permit-as-a-self-employed-person" data-component-id="ind2:heading" class="ind-heading ind-heading--h2">
      Application for a residence permit as a self-employed person
  </h2>

  
  

  
  

  <p>This required amount is valid from 1 July 2026 up to and including 31 December 2026.</p><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross profit per month (with holiday allowance)</td><td>€ 1,766.77</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<div class="ind:clear-both"></div>




          
      </section>


  






<section class="ind-flow ind-section" data-component-id="ind2:section">
      
                              




<h2 id="application-for-a-residence-permit-seafaring-service" data-component-id="ind2:heading" class="ind-heading ind-heading--h2">
      Application for a residence permit seafaring service
  </h2>

  
  

  
  

  <h3>Required amount 2026</h3><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Required amount per month</td><td>$ 690</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<div class="ind:clear-both"></div>




          
      </section>


  






<section class="ind-flow ind-section" data-component-id="ind2:section">
      
                              




<h2 id="application-for-a-residence-permit-as-an-au-pair" data-component-id="ind2:heading" class="ind-heading ind-heading--h2">
      Application for a residence permit as an au pair
  </h2>

  
  

  
  

  <p>These required amounts are valid from 1 July 2026 up to and including 31 December 2026.</p><h3>​Host family of a married/unmarried couple living together</h3><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 3,505.50</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 3,785.94</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p><h3>Host family of single parent</h3><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 2,804.40</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 3,028.75</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p>

<div class="ind:clear-both"></div>




          
      </section>


  






<section class="ind-flow ind-section" data-component-id="ind2:section">
      
                              




<h2 id="application-for-a-residence-permit-for-medical-treatment" data-component-id="ind2:heading" class="ind-heading ind-heading--h2">
      Application for a residence permit for medical treatment
  </h2>

  
  

  
  

  <p>These required amounts are valid from 1 July 2026 up to and including 31 December 2026.</p><h3>​You are married/registered partners or an unmarried couple living together and your partner comes to the Netherlands with you ​</h3><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 2,337.00</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 2,523.96</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p><h3>You are single or a single parent and your child comes to the Netherlands with you</h3><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>​​Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 1,635.90</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 1,766.77</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p>

<div class="ind:clear-both"></div>




          
      </section>


  






<section class="ind-flow ind-section" data-component-id="ind2:section">
      
                              




<h2 id="a-person-in-the-netherlands-financier-pays-your-stay-for-medical-treatment" data-component-id="ind2:heading" class="ind-heading ind-heading--h2">
      A person in the Netherlands (financier) pays your stay for medical treatment
  </h2>

  
  

  
  

  <p>These required amounts are valid from 1 July 2026 up to and including 31 December 2026.</p><h3>Family situation financier: married/registered partner or unmarried partners living together<br>Family situation foreign national: single or single parent (child comes to the Netherlands)​</h3><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 4,440.30</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 4,795.52</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p><h3>Family situation financier: &nbsp;married/registered partner or unmarried partners living together<br>Family situation foreign national: married/registered partner or unmarried partners living together (partner comes to the Netherlands)</h3><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 4,674.00</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 5,047.92</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p><h3>Family situation financier: single or single parent<br>Family situation foreign national: married/registered partner or unmarried partners living together (partner comes to the Netherlands) ​​</h3><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 3,972.90</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 4,290.73</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p><h3>Family situation financier: single or single parent<br>Family situation foreign national: single or single parent (child comes to the Netherlands)</h3><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 3,739.20</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 4,038.33</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p>

<div class="ind:clear-both"></div>




          
      </section>


  






<section class="ind-flow ind-section" data-component-id="ind2:section">
      
                              




<h2 id="application-for-a-permanent-residence-permit-or-residence-permit-for-long-term-eu-residents" data-component-id="ind2:heading" class="ind-heading ind-heading--h2">
      Application for a permanent residence permit or residence permit for long-term EU residents
  </h2>

  
  

  
  

  <p>These required amounts are valid from 1 July 2026 up to and including 31 December 2026.</p><h3>​You yourself show income</h3><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 1,635.90</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 1,766.77</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p><h3>A family member shows income ​​</h3><h4>Your family member is married/registered partner or unmarried partner living together</h4><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 2,337.00</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 2,523.96</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p><h4>Your family member is a single parent&nbsp;​</h4><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 1,635.90</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 1,766.77</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p>

<div class="ind:clear-both"></div>




          
      </section>


  






<section class="ind-flow ind-section" data-component-id="ind2:section">
      
                              




<h2 id="application-for-other-residence-permits" data-component-id="ind2:heading" class="ind-heading ind-heading--h2">
      Application for other residence permits
  </h2>

  
  

  
  

  <p>These required amounts are valid from 1 July 2026 up to and including 31 December 2026.</p><h3>You are married/registered partner or unmarried partner living together&nbsp;</h3><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV&nbsp;salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 2,337.00</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 2,523.96</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p><h3>​You are single or a single parent</h3><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><tbody><tr><td>Gross SV&nbsp;salary per month without holiday allowance</td><td>€ 1,635.90</td></tr><tr><td>Gross SV salary per month with holiday allowance</td><td>€ 1,766.77</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p>

<div class="ind:clear-both"></div>




          
      </section>


  






<section class="ind-flow ind-section" data-component-id="ind2:section">
      
                              




<h2 id="required-amounts-previous-3-years" data-component-id="ind2:heading" class="ind-heading ind-heading--h2">
      Required amounts previous 3 years
  </h2>

  
  

  
  

  <p>The IND uses former required amounts sometimes to decide if your income is sustainable. For example, because your income amount is not the same every month. Or because your labour contract is valid for less than 6 months on the date of application for a residence permit. The tables show the required amounts for the past 3 years.</p><h3>​Tabel old required amounts: spouses or unmarried&nbsp;couples living together&nbsp;</h3><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">​Period</th><th scope="col">​Gross SV salary a month<br>without holiday allowance</th><th scope="col">​Gross SV salary a month<br>with holiday allowance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">1 January 2026 up to and including 30 June 2026</th><td>€ 2,294.40</td><td>€ 2,477.95</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">1 July 2025 up to and including 31 December 2025</th><td>€ 2,245.80</td><td>€ 2,425.46</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">1 January 2025 up to and including 30 June 2025</th><td>€ 2,191.80</td><td>€ 2,367.14</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">1 July 2024 up to and including 31 December 2024</th><td>€ 2,133.60</td><td>€ 2,304.29</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">1 January 2024 up to and including 30 June 2024</th><td>€ 2,069.40</td><td>€ 2,234.95</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">1 July 2023&nbsp;up to and including 31 December 2023</th><td>€ 1.995,00</td><td>€ 2.154,60</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">1 January&nbsp;2023&nbsp;up to and including 30 June&nbsp;2023</th><td>€ 1.934,40</td><td>€ 2.089,16</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p><h3>Tabel old required amounts: single persons or single parents</h3><div class="ind-table-wrapper"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">​Period</th><th scope="col">​Gross SV salary a month<br>without holiday allowance</th><th scope="col">​Gross SV salary a month<br>with holiday allowance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">1 January 2026 up to and including 30 June 2026</th><td>€ 1,606.08</td><td>€ 1,734.57</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">1 July 2025 up to and including 31 December 2025</th><td>€ 1,572.06</td><td>€ 1,697.82</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">1 January 2025 up to and including 30 June 2025</th><td>€ 1,534.26</td><td>€ 1,657.00</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">1 July 2024 up to and including 31 December 2024</th><td>€ 1,493.52</td><td>€ 1,613.00</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">1 January 2024 up to and including 30 June 2024</th><td>€ 1,448.58</td><td>€ 1,564.47</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">​1 July 2023&nbsp;up to and including 31 December 2023</th><td>€ 1.396,50</td><td>€ 1.508,22</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">1 January&nbsp;2023&nbsp;up to and including 30 June&nbsp;2023</th><td>€ 1.354,08</td><td>€ 1.462,41</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>SV salary is the social security salary (in Dutch: sociaalverzekeringsloon or sv-loon in short). This is the gross salary on which wage tax and national insurance contributions (for unemployment, sickness and incapacity for work benefits)are calculated. The SV salary is on your payslip.</p>

<div class="ind:clear-both"></div>




          
      </section>


  






